 "about_text": "Lisson Gallery is an internationally established contemporary art gallery founded in 1967 by Nicholas Logsdail, with roots in Minimal and Conceptual art. Today it represents more than 70 artists spanning generations and geographies, from postwar figures like Carl Andre and Sol LeWitt to contemporary names such as Ai Weiwei, Marina Abramović and Hiroshi Sugimoto. Its Los Angeles space opened in 2023 in Hollywood's Sycamore District, occupying a standalone two-story building of over 8,000 square feet, with an inaugural exhibition of Carmen Herrera's Days of the Week series. The gallery also maintains spaces in London, New York and Shanghai, continuing its history of introducing international artists to new audiences.",
